.TH SDL_HINT_TIMER_RESOLUTION 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_TIMER_RESOLUTION \- A variable that controls the timer resolution, in milliseconds.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_TIMER_RESOLUTION \(dqSDL_TIMER_RESOLUTION\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The higher resolution the timer, the more frequently the CPU services timer interrupts, and the more precise delays are, but this takes up power and CPU time\[char46] This hint is only used on Windows\[char46]
.PP
See this blog post for more information: http://randomascii\[char46]wordpress\[char46]com/2013/07/08/windows-timer-resolution-megawatts-wasted/
.PP
The default value is \(dq1\(dq\[char46]
.PP
If this variable is set to \(dq0\(dq, the system timer resolution is not set\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

